# The build context of the Dockerfile next to this file: an allowlist.
#
# The first rule excludes everything; the rules after it let in exactly what
# the image is built from -- the runtime lock, the lock of the pip that
# installs it, the lock of psycopg-c's build tools and the four scripts that
# fetch and install them during the build without being copied
# (DB/fetch_verified.py, DB/install_pip.py, DB/install_locked.py and
# DB/locked_files.py), the Python modules of the people_pubs package,
# the three demonstration fixtures with their README, the four files of the
# schema bootstrap in DB/init/, the two Compose files, create_secrets.sh,
# set_passwords.sh and the two licences. Nothing else in
# the checkout reaches the build context or the image, wherever it lies: not
# .git, environment files or secret files, database data or backups, virtual
# environments, caches, local notes or any other file in DB/init/. A new file
# the image needs has to be added here and copied in the Dockerfile
# explicitly.
*
!DB/requirements-pip.txt
!DB/requirements-build.txt
!DB/requirements.txt
!DB/fetch_verified.py
!DB/install_pip.py
!DB/install_locked.py
!DB/locked_files.py
!DB/people_pubs/**/*.py
!DB/tests/fixtures/golden/README.md
!DB/tests/fixtures/golden/demo_roster_minimal.csv
!DB/tests/fixtures/golden/orcid_work_minimal.json
!DB/tests/fixtures/golden/crossref_work_minimal.json
!DB/init/000_init.sql
!DB/init/010_ingestion_runtime_schema.sql
!DB/init/011_member_info_manual.sql
!DB/init/020_role_passwords.sh
!compose.yaml
!compose.postgres-port.yaml
!create_secrets.sh
!set_passwords.sh
!LICENSE
!LICENSE-CC-BY-4.0
